sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: docs/reference/tasks.md#check-an-external-group, the shape guide (official `@swamp/ssh exec`), the publish chart for the handoff push.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rule 22 (no shipped scripts: every task VM step is one `@swamp/ssh exec` argv, 209 shapes the outputs in TypeScript; no step copies a script to the VM), rule 16 (no snapshot after the push: the import checks the bundled commit and tree).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: tasks:check
  %% kind: tasks.check
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Task VM<br/>reached over ssh
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>repo · Checks
  CLI->>GW: tasks:check 42<br/>--subtask=7 --phase=handoff
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit tasks:check 42 --subtask=7 --phase=handoff`
  %%> - syntax: `<group> --subtask=<id> --phase=baseline|handoff [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  Note over GW: Admit the check<br/>check 17 · task #5170
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - group 42 is open and external, with its own task VM workspace, else `tasks.no_workspace`
  %%> - subtask 7 is the current open subtask, else `tasks.subtask_not_current`
  %%> - a baseline only before any implementer started, else `tasks.baseline_done`
  %%> Result:
  %%> - check 17 recorded as running; the full intent holds the Project check, setup (baseline), deliverables (handoff), base commit and the VM's SSH target
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-check
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the intent, and vault key names for the CI tokens when the Project requires handoff CI
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5170
  Note over SW: Build every argv<br/>prepare · paths checked
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - TypeScript on 209 builds each step's `@swamp/ssh exec` argv from the intent
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - an absolute or `..` deliverable directory, a non-canonical overlay path, or a `fails_on_base` command without a base commit: `tasks.deliverable_invalid`, before any command
  opt baseline with setup steps
    SW->>N: Run setup in order<br/>setup-0, setup-1, …
    %%> How:
    %%> - each is `env -C <checkout> … /bin/bash -lc <command>` with its own timeout; `@orbit/ci-caches` expands to the shared program
    %%> - a failed step skips the rest and the Project check
  end
  SW->>N: Snapshot the workspace<br/>snapshot-before-* · own index
  %%> How:
  %%> - `git read-tree HEAD`, `git add --all`, `git write-tree` on the run's index file, and `git rev-parse HEAD`; the real index is untouched
  SW->>N: Run the Project check<br/>project · bash -lc
  %%> How:
  %%> - one argv in the checkout; output stays in native history on 209, the result keeps a redacted 16 KiB tail
  opt handoff with deliverables
    SW->>N: Run each deliverable<br/>diff · base-N · deliverable-N
    %%> How:
    %%> - `diff`: `git diff-tree -r --no-renames --name-status -z <base> <tree>` for file deliverables
    %%> - a `fails_on_base` command first runs on its start commit: `git archive`, `tar -x`, a copy of installed `vendor` and `node_modules`, the declared test paths, then the command
    %%> Refuses:
    %%> - a missing overlay file or directory: `tasks.deliverable_invalid`
  end
  SW->>N: Snapshot the checked tree<br/>snapshot-after-* · changed
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - a moved tree makes the check `changed`; a failed command or unmet deliverable makes it `failed`
  opt passed handoff
    SW->>N: Commit the candidate<br/>git commit · check-operations ref
    %%> How:
    %%> - `git add --all`, one `git commit` as Orbit with hooks off, `git rev-parse HEAD HEAD^{tree} HEAD^`
    %%> - 209 checks the tree and parent equal the checked snapshot, else `changed`; then `git update-ref refs/orbit/check-operations/<operation>`
  end
  opt Project requires handoff CI
    SW->>GH: Push the candidate<br/>task-42-handoff · no force
    %%> How:
    %%> - export, import, mint, push and revoke as in `tasks:publish`; the run then ends with CI pending
    %%> - a native schedule reads the Checks once a minute, snapshots the workspace again and settles the check
  end
  alt every step passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>outcome · commit · ci
    Note over GW: Record check 17<br/>passed, failed or changed
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or no reply
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Mark the task failed<br/>check 17 failed
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5170
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
